<title>BELGIUM: EU to review U.S. malt barley, rice rows Feb 5.</title>
<headline>EU to review U.S. malt barley, rice rows Feb 5.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union trade officials will meet again in the so-called &quot;Article 113 Committee&quot; on February 5 to discuss malting barley and rice trade problems with the U.S., EU officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>They said that the European Commission will present a report on a cumulative rice recovery system allowing traders to claw back payment of excess duties.</p>
<p>Washington is also annoyed by the EU's delay in opening a 30,000 tonnes annual reduced tariff quota on imports of U.S. malting barley.</p>
<p>It has warned that if no a action is taken it will file a complaint to the Geneva-based World Trade Organisation towards the end of February.</p>
</text>
